{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRecordingTrunc","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRecordingTrunc","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedStandardCount","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRecordingIndex"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppendSteps_qPositions_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppendSteps_qPositions_self","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L251-L257","doc":"**The recording tableau is determined by its positions.** Once the horizon clears every entry,\nthe replay is `Q` on the nose — the form the RSK inverse consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppendSteps_qPositions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppendSteps_qPositions","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L237-L249","doc":"**The replay is exact.** Appending the timestamps below `n` at the positions read off `Q`\nrebuilds `Q`'s truncation at `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppendSteps_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppendSteps_append","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L227-L235","doc":"A run of appends, one step peeled off the end. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppend_qTrunc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qAppend_qTrunc","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L168-L225","doc":"**One step of the replay.** Writing timestamp `t` at the end of its row in `qTrunc Q t` produces\n`qTrunc Q (t + 1)`.\n\nThe two cases at the top row are the whole content. When the top row holds nothing below `t` the\ntruncation is empty and `t` starts the tableau — and then no row below can hold anything below\n`t + 1` either, because column strictness would put a smaller entry in the top row. Otherwise the\ntop row survives and `t` is appended to it, the rows below being untouched because `t` occurs once.\nBelow the top row the argument recurses, with `exists_le_head` supplying the fact that the top row\nis still non-empty so the index has not shifted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_mem_flatten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_mem_flatten","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L162-L166","doc":"Row membership gives membership in the flattening. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_le_head","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_le_head","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L144-L160","doc":"Any row entry lies at or above an entry of the **top** row. Chaining the previous lemma down the\ncolumn-strict tower, this is what makes a truncation's non-empty rows an initial segment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_lt_of_strictBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_lt_of_strictBelow","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L135-L142","doc":"A row entry witnesses a strictly smaller entry in the row above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_succ_of_not_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_succ_of_not_mem","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L127-L133","doc":"Raising the horizon past a timestamp no row holds changes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_succ_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_succ_mem","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L103-L125","doc":"**A timestamp joins its row at the end.** In a strictly increasing row every entry below `t`\nprecedes `t`, so raising the horizon past `t` appends it. This is why the replay can use `qAppend`,\nwhich only ever writes at the end of a row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_succ_not_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_succ_not_mem","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L89-L101","doc":"Raising the horizon past a timestamp the row does not hold changes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_of_all_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_of_all_lt","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L76-L87","doc":"Past every timestamp the truncation is the tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_zero","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L71-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_eq_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_eq_self","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L64-L69","doc":"Everything is below a horizon that clears the row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_eq_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.filter_lt_eq_nil","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L56-L62","doc":"Nothing is below a zero horizon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_cons","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L52-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc_nil","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qTrunc","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRecordingTrunc.lean#L42-L48","doc":"**The horizon truncation.** `qTrunc Q n` keeps the timestamps of `Q` below `n`, stopping at the\nfirst row that has emptied. On a standard tableau the emptied rows are exactly the bottom ones, so\nstopping at the first is the same as dropping them all — and it keeps the recursion structural. ","signatureChunk":0}]}